UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":1,"title":"Acute Transverse Myelitis","body":"**Recent diving or rapid ascent?** New myelopathy may represent [spinal decompression illness](#/tree/decompression-sickness). Start high-concentration oxygen and contact hyperbaric/diving medicine immediately. Do not delay indicated recompression for routine spinal MRI. Suspected traumatic or compressive pathology still requires urgent targeted evaluation in parallel. [16]\n\n**Transverse myelitis (TM)** is an acute inflammatory disorder of the spinal cord producing a band of motor, sensory, and autonomic dysfunction below the lesion. \"Transverse\" = across the cord at one or more segments.\n\n**The triad that says \"this is the cord\":**\n- **Bilateral** motor weakness (para- or quadriparesis)\n- A **sensory level** — a horizontal line below which sensation changes\n- **Sphincter/autonomic** dysfunction (urinary retention is early and common)\n\n**Tempo:** progresses over hours to 21 days, nadir typically 4 hours to a few days. Faster than GBS climbs, but unlike stroke it is not maximal at onset.\n\n**Outside the diving-related exception above, exclude compression before diagnosing inflammation.** A compressive myelopathy (epidural abscess, hematoma, tumor, disc) looks identical and is a neurosurgical emergency. Get the MRI first.","citation":[1,2,16],"next":"tm-presentation","images":[{"src":"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20420%20260%22%20font-family%3D%22sans-serif%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22420%22%20height%3D%22260%22%20fill%3D%22%230f172a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22210%22%20y%3D%2226%22%20fill%3D%22%23e2e8f0%22%20font-size%3D%2216%22%20font-weight%3D%22bold%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3ESensory%20Level%20%E2%80%94%20the%20cord%20hallmark%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Cellipse%20cx%3D%22120%22%20cy%3D%2260%22%20rx%3D%2226%22%20ry%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%231e293b%22%20stroke%3D%22%2364748b%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22104%22%20y%3D%2286%22%20width%3D%2232%22%20height%3D%22120%22%20rx%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%231e293b%22%20stroke%3D%22%2364748b%22%2F%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2270%22%20y1%3D%22140%22%20x2%3D%22170%22%20y2%3D%22140%22%20stroke%3D%22%23f87171%22%20stroke-width%3D%223%22%20stroke-dasharray%3D%226%204%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22178%22%20y%3D%22135%22%20fill%3D%22%23f87171%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%3Esensory%20level%20(e.g.%20T6)%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22178%22%20y%3D%22150%22%20fill%3D%22%2394a3b8%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%3Enormal%20ABOVE%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22178%22%20y%3D%22178%22%20fill%3D%22%2394a3b8%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%3Enumb%20%2F%20weak%20BELOW%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22300%22%20y%3D%2240%22%20width%3D%22100%22%20height%3D%22180%22%20rx%3D%228%22%20fill%3D%22%231e293b%22%20stroke%3D%22%2364748b%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22350%22%20y%3D%2262%22%20fill%3D%22%23e2e8f0%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20font-weight%3D%22bold%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3ECord%20cross-section%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Cpath%20d%3D%22M350%2090%20q-30%2020%200%2040%20q30%20-20%200%20-40%22%20fill%3D%22%23334155%22%20stroke%3D%22%2394a3b8%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22350%22%20cy%3D%22110%22%20r%3D%2222%22%20fill%3D%22none%22%20stroke%3D%22%23fbbf24%22%20stroke-width%3D%222%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22350%22%20y%3D%22160%22%20fill%3D%22%23fbbf24%22%20font-size%3D%2210%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Einflammation%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22350%22%20y%3D%22174%22%20fill%3D%22%23fbbf24%22%20font-size%3D%2210%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Eacross%20cord%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E","alt":"Schematic of a sensory level: normal sensation above a horizontal line on the trunk, impaired below, with an inflamed spinal cord cross-section.","caption":"A sensory level localizes the lesion to the cord. Map it on the trunk and check for urinary retention. (Original schematic, no license restriction.)"}],"summary":"Acute cord inflammation: bilateral weakness + sensory level + sphincter dysfunction. Diving-related spinal DCI: urgent recompression evaluation; otherwise exclude compression first."}'::jsonb
